---@class opensearch.CreateRequest
---@field index string Name of the data stream or index to target. If the target doesn't exist and matches the name or wildcard (`*`) pattern of an index template with a `data_stream` definition, this request creates the data stream. If the target doesn't exist and doesn't match a data stream template, this request creates the index.
---@field id string The unique identifier for the document.
---@field pipeline? string ID of the pipeline to use to preprocess incoming documents. If the index has a default ingest pipeline specified, then setting the value to `_none` disables the default ingest pipeline for this request. If a final pipeline is configured it will always run, regardless of the value of this parameter.
---@field refresh? opensearch.CommonRefresh If `true`, OpenSearch refreshes the affected shards to make this operation visible to search, if `wait_for` then wait for a refresh to make this operation visible to search, if `false` do nothing with refreshes. Valid values: `true`, `false`, `wait_for`.
---@field routing? opensearch.CommonStringOrStringArray A custom value used to route operations to a specific shard.
---@field timeout? string Period the request waits for the following operations: automatic index creation, dynamic mapping updates, waiting for active shards.
---@field version? number Explicit version number for concurrency control. The specified version must match the current version of the document for the request to succeed.
---@field version_type? string The specific version type: `external`, `external_gte`.
---@field wait_for_active_shards? opensearch.CommonWaitForActiveShards The number of shard copies that must be active before proceeding with the operation. Set to `all` or any positive integer up to the total number of shards in the index (`number_of_replicas+1`).
---@field pretty? boolean Whether to pretty-format the returned JSON response.
---@field human? boolean Whether to return human-readable values for statistics.
---@field error_trace? boolean Whether to include the stack trace of returned errors.
---@field source? string The URL-encoded request definition. Useful for libraries that do not accept a request body for non-POST requests.
---@field filter_path? opensearch.CommonStringOrStringArray A comma-separated list of filters used to filter the response. Use wildcards to match any field or part of a field's name. To exclude fields, use `-`.
---@field document any The document to index, sent as the whole request body.

