---The index lifecycle management configuration.
---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsLifecycle
---@field name string
---@field indexing_complete? opensearch.CommonStringifiedBoolean
---@field origination_date? opensearch.CommonStringifiedEpochTimeUnitMillis The timestamp used to calculate the index age for its phase transitions. Use this setting if you create a new index that contains old data and want to use the original creation date to calculate the index age. Specified as a Unix epoch value in milliseconds.
---@field parse_origination_date? boolean When `true`, parses the origination date from the index name. This origination date is used to calculate the index age for its phase transitions. The index name must match the pattern `^.*-{date_format}-\\d+`, where the `date_format` is `yyyy.MM.dd` and the trailing digits are optional. An index that was rolled over would normally match the full format, for example `logs-2016.10.31-000002`). If the index name doesn't match the pattern, index creation fails.
---@field step? opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsLifecycleStep
---@field rollover_alias? string The index alias to update when the index rolls over. Specify when using a policy that contains a rollover action. When the index rolls over, the alias is updated to reflect that the index is no longer the write index. For more information about rolling indexes, see Rollover.

