---Limits applied to dynamically created Lucene fields.
---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingDynamicPropertiesLuceneField
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong The maximum number of dynamically created Lucene fields allowed.

---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingLimitDepth
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong The maximum depth for a field, which is measured as the number of inner objects. For instance, if all fields are defined at the root object level, then the depth is `1`. If there is one object mapping, then the depth is `2`.

---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingLimitDimensionFields
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong [preview] This functionality is in technical preview and may be changed or removed in a future release. OpenSearch will work to fix any issues, but features in technical preview are not subject to the support SLA of official GA features.

---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingLimitFieldNameLength
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong Setting for the maximum length of a field name. This setting isn't really something that addresses mappings explosion but might still be useful if you want to limit the field length. It usually shouldn't be necessary to set this setting. The default is okay unless a user starts to add a huge number of fields with really long names. Default is `Long.MAX_VALUE` (no limit).

---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingLimitNestedFields
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong The maximum number of distinct nested mappings in an index. The nested type should only be used in special cases, when arrays of objects need to be queried independently of each other. To safeguard against poorly designed mappings, this setting limits the number of unique nested types per index.

---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingLimitNestedObjects
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong The maximum number of nested JSON objects that a single document can contain across all nested types. This limit helps to prevent out of memory errors when a document contains too many nested objects.

---@class opensearch.IndicesCommonIndexSettingsMappingLimitTotalFields
---@field limit? opensearch.CommonStringifiedLong The maximum number of fields in an index. Field and object mappings, as well as field aliases count towards this limit. The limit is in place to prevent mappings and searches from becoming too large. Higher values can lead to performance degradations and memory issues, especially in clusters with a high load or few resources.

