---@class opensearch.MsearchByIndexRequest
---@field index string A comma-separated list of data streams, indexes, and index aliases to search.
---@field allow_partial_results? boolean Specifies whether to return partial results if there are shard request timeouts or shard failures
---@field ccs_minimize_roundtrips? boolean If `true`, network round-trips between the coordinating node and remote clusters are minimized for cross-cluster search requests.
---@field max_concurrent_searches? number Maximum number of concurrent searches the multi search API can execute.
---@field max_concurrent_shard_requests? number Maximum number of concurrent shard requests that each sub-search request executes per node.
---@field pre_filter_shard_size? number Defines a threshold that enforces a pre-filter roundtrip to prefilter search shards based on query rewriting if the number of shards the search request expands to exceeds the threshold. This filter roundtrip can limit the number of shards significantly if for instance a shard can not match any documents based on its rewrite method i.e., if date filters are mandatory to match but the shard bounds and the query are disjoint.
---@field rest_total_hits_as_int? boolean If `true`, `hits.total` are returned as an integer in the response. Defaults to false, which returns an object.
---@field search_type? string Indicates whether global term and document frequencies should be used when scoring returned documents.
---@field typed_keys? boolean Specifies whether aggregation and suggester names should be prefixed by their respective types in the response.
---@field pretty? boolean Whether to pretty-format the returned JSON response.
---@field human? boolean Whether to return human-readable values for statistics.
---@field error_trace? boolean Whether to include the stack trace of returned errors.
---@field source? string The URL-encoded request definition. Useful for libraries that do not accept a request body for non-POST requests.
---@field filter_path? opensearch.CommonStringOrStringArray A comma-separated list of filters used to filter the response. Use wildcards to match any field or part of a field's name. To exclude fields, use `-`.
---@field body string Searches as newline-delimited JSON (application/x-ndjson): a header line (`{"index":"logs"}` or `{}`), then the search body line, for each search. End the body with a newline.

