---@class opensearch.SearchTemplateRequest
---@field allow_no_indices? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if any wildcard expression, index alias, or `_all` value targets only missing or closed indexes. This behavior applies even if the request targets other open indexes. For example, a request targeting `foo*,bar*` returns an error if an index starts with `foo` but no index starts with `bar`.
---@field ccs_minimize_roundtrips? boolean If `true`, network round-trips are minimized for cross-cluster search requests.
---@field expand_wildcards? opensearch.CommonExpandWildcards Type of index that wildcard patterns can match. If the request can target data streams, this argument determines whether wildcard expressions match hidden data streams. Supports comma-separated values, such as `open,hidden`. Valid values are: `all`, `open`, `closed`, `hidden`, `none`.
---@field explain? boolean If `true`, the response includes additional details about score computation as part of a hit.
---@field ignore_throttled? boolean If `true`, specified concrete, expanded, or aliased indexes are not included in the response when throttled.
---@field ignore_unavailable? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if it targets a missing or closed index.
---@field phase_took? boolean Indicates whether to return phase-level `took` time values in the response.
---@field preference? string Specifies the node or shard the operation should be performed on. Random by default.
---@field profile? boolean If `true`, the query execution is profiled.
---@field rest_total_hits_as_int? boolean If `true`, `hits.total` are rendered as an integer in the response.
---@field routing? opensearch.CommonStringOrStringArray A custom value used to route operations to a specific shard.
---@field scroll? string Specifies how long a consistent view of the index should be maintained for scrolled search.
---@field search_pipeline? string Customizable sequence of processing stages applied to search queries.
---@field search_type? string The type of the search operation.
---@field typed_keys? boolean If `true`, the response prefixes aggregation and suggester names with their respective types.
---@field pretty? boolean Whether to pretty-format the returned JSON response.
---@field human? boolean Whether to return human-readable values for statistics.
---@field error_trace? boolean Whether to include the stack trace of returned errors.
