---@class opensearch.UpdateByQueryRequest
---@field index string A comma-separated list of data streams, indexes, and aliases to search. Supports wildcards (`*`). To search all data streams or indexes, omit this parameter or use `*` or `_all`.
---@field _source? opensearch.CoreSearchSourceConfigParam Set to `true` or `false` to return the `_source` field or not, or a list of fields to return.
---@field _source_excludes? opensearch.UpdateByQueryRequestSourceExcludesList List of fields to exclude from the returned `_source` field.
---@field _source_includes? opensearch.UpdateByQueryRequestSourceIncludesList List of fields to extract and return from the `_source` field.
---@field allow_no_indices? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if any wildcard expression, index alias, or `_all` value targets only missing or closed indexes. This behavior applies even if the request targets other open indexes. For example, a request targeting `foo*,bar*` returns an error if an index starts with `foo` but no index starts with `bar`.
---@field analyze_wildcard? boolean If `true`, wildcard and prefix queries are analyzed.
---@field analyzer? string Analyzer to use for the query string.
---@field conflicts? string What to do if update by query hits version conflicts: `abort` or `proceed`.
---@field default_operator? opensearch.CommonQueryDslOperator|string The default operator for query string query: `AND` or `OR`.
---@field df? string Field to use as default where no field prefix is given in the query string.
---@field expand_wildcards? opensearch.CommonExpandWildcards Type of index that wildcard patterns can match. If the request can target data streams, this argument determines whether wildcard expressions match hidden data streams. Supports comma-separated values, such as `open,hidden`. Valid values are: `all`, `open`, `closed`, `hidden`, `none`.
---@field from? number Starting offset.
---@field ignore_unavailable? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if it targets a missing or closed index.
---@field lenient? boolean If `true`, format-based query failures (such as providing text to a numeric field) in the query string will be ignored.
---@field max_docs? number Maximum number of documents to process. Defaults to all documents.
---@field pipeline? string ID of the pipeline to use to preprocess incoming documents. If the index has a default ingest pipeline specified, then setting the value to `_none` disables the default ingest pipeline for this request. If a final pipeline is configured it will always run, regardless of the value of this parameter.
---@field preference? string Specifies the node or shard the operation should be performed on. Random by default.
---@field q? string Query in the Lucene query string syntax.
---@field refresh? opensearch.CommonRefresh If `true`, OpenSearch refreshes affected shards to make the operation visible to search.
---@field request_cache? boolean If `true`, the request cache is used for this request.
---@field requests_per_second? number The throttle for this request in sub-requests per second.
---@field routing? opensearch.CommonStringOrStringArray A custom value used to route operations to a specific shard.
---@field scroll? string Period to retain the search context for scrolling.
---@field scroll_size? number Size of the scroll request that powers the operation.
---@field search_timeout? string Explicit timeout for each search request.
---@field search_type? string The type of the search operation. Available options: `query_then_fetch`, `dfs_query_then_fetch`.
---@field size? number Deprecated, use `max_docs` instead.
---@field slices? opensearch.CommonSlices The number of slices this task should be divided into.
---@field sort? opensearch.UpdateByQueryRequestSortList A comma-separated list of <field>:<direction> pairs.
---@field stats? opensearch.UpdateByQueryRequestStatsList Specific `tag` of the request for logging and statistical purposes.
---@field terminate_after? number Maximum number of documents to collect for each shard. If a query reaches this limit, OpenSearch terminates the query early. OpenSearch collects documents before sorting. Use with caution. OpenSearch applies this parameter to each shard handling the request. When possible, let OpenSearch perform early termination automatically. Avoid specifying this parameter for requests that target data streams with backing indexes across multiple data tiers.
---@field timeout? string Period each update request waits for the following operations: dynamic mapping updates, waiting for active shards.
---@field version? boolean If `true`, returns the document version as part of a hit.
---@field wait_for_active_shards? opensearch.CommonWaitForActiveShards The number of shard copies that must be active before proceeding with the operation. Set to `all` or any positive integer up to the total number of shards in the index (`number_of_replicas+1`).
---@field wait_for_completion? boolean If `true`, the request blocks until the operation is complete.
